   00494|     assert_eq!(coding_records, 115, "coding-path regression floor");
   00495|     assert_eq!(committed_gaps(root), expected_gaps);
   00496|     // The floor moves with the closure, not with the handlers: every gap added
   00497|     // under issue #1021 is a `closure-generated-*.lino` record for a token the
   00498|     // new prose pulled into the total closure -- 74 for the contribution
   00499|     // artifacts, then 16 more when the listing detector was given its Spanish
   00500|     // vocabulary (`lista`, `ficheros`, `archivos`, `aqui`, ...), then 8 more
   00501|     // for the closed-class words the language-less coding request subtracts
   00502|     // (`me`, `my`, `our`, `we`, `some`, `these`, `just`) plus the Spanish
   00503|     // `guion`, and one more for `copy_stdin_to_stdout` once the portable seed
   00504|     // bundle started naming the task issue #863 reported. A new language's
   00505|     // words arriving as generated closure records rather than as hand-written
   00506|     // gaps is the shape this floor exists to show; `request_function_word`
   00507|     // joins the count as a hand-written record because every meaning in
   00508|     // `data/seed/meanings.lino` -- all 22 of them, not just the new one --
   00509|     // carries its lexemes without the five-field metadata that file has never
   00510|     // supplied. The last twelve arrived the same way: the verified-mutating-
   00511|     // action responses issues #824 and #944 added pull their two intent tokens
   00512|     // and their ten response ids into the closure, and every one of the twelve
   00513|     // is a `closure-generated-*.lino` record -- no hand-written gap, no
   00514|     // handler without metadata. The one after them is hand-written and says so
   00515|     // honestly: `file_leading_line_constraint` in
   00516|     // `data/seed/meanings-file-write.lino` is the vocabulary for "the first
   00517|     // line must be ..." that lets an evidence-record request pin its opening
   00518|     // line (issue #1066), and that file, like `data/seed/meanings.lino`, has
   00519|     // never carried the five fields for any of its records. A gap recorded in
   00520|     // reviewed data is the outcome this audit is for; the floor above is what
   00521|     // forbids the same omission on the coding path.
   00522|     //
   00523|     // The seven after it are closure records again, and they arrived for the
   00524|     // same reason the twelve before them did. `data/seed/meanings-note-
   00525|     // composition.lino` carries both of its meanings with all five fields --
   00526|     // it is a hand-written file and it is complete -- but the closure expands
   00527|     // each of its English surfaces into a generated record, and `produce`,
   00528|     // `compose`, `draft`, `assemble`, `prepare`, `note` and `memo` had no
   00529|     // generated record before. `report`, `summary` and `brief` already did.
   00530|     // Vocabulary for a new capability entering the closure is exactly the
   00531|     // shape this number tracks: described data grows the count, an
   00532|     // undescribed handler would not be allowed to.
   00533|     //
   00534|     // The eleven after those are the same two shapes again, and they arrived
   00535|     // together under issue #1066. Ten are closure records for the honest
   00536|     // replies a decomposition gives when it cannot enumerate anything: the two
   00537|     // intent tokens `task_decomposition_single_need` and
   00538|     // `task_decomposition_unsplit_depth_bound`, and their eight response ids,
   00539|     // one per language the seed then answered in. The eleventh is hand-written
   00540|     // and says so:
   00541|     // `file_write_deferred_content` in `data/seed/meanings-file-write.lino` is
   00542|     // the vocabulary for a payload that *names* the work product ("... the
   00543|     // findings", "... 结论") rather than stating it, which is what stops a
   00544|     // request to record findings from writing the words "the findings" into
   00545|     // the caller's file. That file carries `role` and has never carried the
   00546|     // other four for any record, so the new one is a gap on exactly the terms
   00547|     // its neighbours already are.
   00548|     // The thirteen after those are one response id per decomposition intent,
   00549|     // and they arrived when Spanish stopped being answered in English (issue
   00550|     // #1066). `es` is a registered language, `data/seed/multilingual-responses-
   00551|     // decomposition.lino` carried no record in it, and `localized_response`
   00552|     // falls back to English rather than failing -- so a Spanish speaker asking
   00553|     // why nothing could be enumerated was told something true in words they had
   00554|     // not asked in. Filling the hole is described data entering the closure,
   00555|     // which is the growth this number exists to track. Leaving the fallback in
   00556|     // place would have held the count still and kept the answer wrong, which is
   00557|     // the direction this floor is here to make visible.
   00558|     // Issue #1069 first contributes 33 more reviewed closure gaps: the two new
   00559|     // repository-observation intents and ten localized response ids, plus the
   00560|     // source-search vocabulary generated from the 29 complete coding records
   00561|     // above. The exact-composition, failed multi-read and link-publish response
   00562|     // seeds then add 18 generated records while displacing the three obsolete
   00563|     // render-surface tokens, for a net 15 more gaps. They are closure data, not
   00564|     // missing metadata on the coding path. Six more arrive with the member-list
   00565|     // kinds: `set`, `collection`, `group`, `lists`, `sequence` and
   00566|     // `alternation` are the English surfaces that let a request name the
   00567|     // collection it edits, and the closure expands each into a generated
   00568|     // record. Vocabulary for a new capability entering the closure is the same
   00569|     // shape as every addition above it.
   00570|     // The last 24 are the sentences a change route says its change in, and they
   00571|     // are four intents plus one response id per registered language for each:
